<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 22,151,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 22,151,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members</p>
<p>(crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 09/25/96    09/18/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 22,151,000  22,921,000   24,465,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	33,990,000  33,990,000   33,842,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,637,015  34,637,015	    N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  54,813	34,444	    N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA.</p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   09/25/96    09/18/96    Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,291,000   3,804,000    4,805,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    3,653,000   3,902,000    4,073,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,808,000   3,877,000    4,326,000</p>
<p> South Central    1,502,000   1,470,000    1,788,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,348,000   3,105,000    2,759,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,888,000   4,983,000    4,792,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,661,000   1,780,000    1,922,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	22,151,000  22,921,000   24,465,000</p>
